# Files NOT uploaded by `gcloud app deploy`. Allowlist: ignore everything, then
# re-include only what the App Engine Go build needs (the source and the SQL it reads).
# Cloud Build downloads the public Go modules itself, so there is no vendor/. Nothing else belongs in the upload:
# .env, token.json, databases, logs and binaries were being uploaded before, which
# both slowed every deploy (a 31 MB binary changes on each build) and copied
# credentials into the staging bucket. Runtime config comes from the GCS config object
# (config/env), not from a file in the upload.
*

!cmd/
!cmd/**
!pkg/
!pkg/**
!sql/
!sql/**
!go.mod
!go.sum

# .env is deliberately not re-included: the app is configured from gs://<bucket>/config/env.
# TestGAEUploadNeverIncludesDotEnv fails if a rule here would upload a .env or token file.
# tests are not built into the service
*_test.go
**/testdata/
